  {
   "key": "federal-representatives-314",
   "date": "2006-11-02",
   "house": "representatives",
   "question": "The majority voted in favour of a [motion](http://www.openaustralia.org/debate/?id=2006-11-02.29.2) \"That the time allotted for the remaining stages of the bill be until 1.30 pm this day.\"(Read more about the stages that a bill must pass through [here](http://www.peo.gov.au/learning/fact-sheets/making-a-law.html). ) It was moved by Liberal MP [Tony Abbott](http://publicwhip-rails.openaustraliafoundation.org.au/mp.php?mpn=Tony_Abbott&mpc=Warringah&house=representatives). This division follows Mr Abbott's previous motion that the bill be considered an urgent bill.(Read more about that division [here](http://publicwhip-rails.openaustraliafoundation.org.au/division.php?date=2006-11-02&number=1&dmp=21&house=representatives). ) _Background to the bill_ The bill was introduced to allow the federal government to sell its interest in [Medibank Private](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Medibank_Private) Limited and allow Medibank to operate on a “for profit” basis. The Coalition Government plans to do this after the 2007 election, should it be re-elected.(Read more about this privatisation proposal on Wikipedia [here](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Medibank_Private#Privatisation_proposals) and on the ABC's World Today program [here](http://www.abc.net.au/worldtoday/content/2006/s1739241.htm).)",
   "stage": "Allotment of Time",
